---
layout: base.njk
title: "The Jars Revealed"
summary: "What was in the two jars you scanned on the Natural Trace stand."
permalink: /scan/
# The page behind the QR code on the physical stand. It is deliberately
# unlinked from the navigation, kept out of the sitemap (the exclusion below is
# what does that; see src/sitemap.njk) and marked noindex, because a search
# visitor landing on "you scanned the jars" with no jars in front of them would
# only be confused.
#
# One page covering both jars, from 24 Aug 2026. It was a page per jar with a
# code per jar until Alrik asked for a single code, which also matches the
# printed stand card: that card already carries one QR, not two. The cost is
# that the counter can no longer say which jar drew the scan, because there is
# now only one thing to scan. docs/qr-scan-tracking.md records the trade.
#
# Scan counting happens before this page loads, in the Cloudflare worker under
# qr/. Nothing on this page tracks anything.
bodyClass: page-scan
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
noindex: true
---

{#- Nothing in this hero may name which pile is which. The two cards below are
    a guess, and a heading that gives the answer away first would leave them
    revealing something the reader already knows. -#}
<section class="challenge scan-hero" style="padding-top:9rem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="challenge-grid">
      <div class="challenge-text">
        <span class="section-label">{{ scan.opening.label }}</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">{{ scan.opening.title }}</h2>
        <p class="challenge-lead" style="margin-top:1.5rem">{{ scan.opening.lead }}</p>
        {#- Three lines rather than one sentence, because they are three separate
            observations and reading them as a list is the point. -#}
        <ul class="scan-identical">
          {% for item in scan.opening.identical %}
          <li>{{ item }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p class="challenge-lead">{{ scan.opening.closing }}</p>
      </div>
      {% if scan.opening.image %}
      <div class="solution-photo">
        <img src="{{ scan.opening.image }}" alt="{{ scan.opening.image_alt }}" width="1000" height="1000">
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The two jars, stated rather than revealed.

    This was a tap-to-reveal until 25 Aug, blurred photographs with the jar name
    over them. It was dropped once the physical stand was photographed: the
    printed card carries a tick beside one jar and a cross beside the other, so
    the answer is on the table before anyone scans anything. A reveal whose
    answer the visitor already holds is theatre, and it competes with our own
    artwork rather than adding to it.

    So the page does the part the card cannot. The card says which jar is
    authentic; this says why that is knowable at all, and why nothing about the
    powder itself could ever have told you. -#}
<section class="scan-reveal">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="scan-cards">
      {% for side in [scan.reveal.left, scan.reveal.right] %}
      <article class="scan-card">
        <div class="scan-shot">
          <img src="{{ side.image }}" alt="{{ side.image_alt }}" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy">
          {#- The jar name stays on the photograph. It is what lets someone
              standing at the stand match a picture to a jar in front of them,
              and on a phone the cards stack so position carries nothing. -#}
          <span class="scan-label">{{ side.label }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="scan-answer">
          <h3>{{ side.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ side.body }}</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="valueprop">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="vp-grid about-grid-2">
      <article class="vp-card">
        <h3>{{ scan.question_title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ scan.question_body }}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="vp-card">
        <h3>{{ scan.answer_title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ scan.answer_body }}</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="finalcta">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="finalcta-inner">
      <h2>{{ scan.cta_heading }}</h2>
      <div class="finalcta-actions">
        <a href="{{ scan.cta_url }}" class="btn btn-white" style="cursor:pointer">{{ scan.cta_text }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
